WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.680
Abraham: With the large amount of
malware out there it will inevitably

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.280
penetrate and infect a system
especially a vulnerable system.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:13.119
This infection maybe caused by downloading
a music file, a video file, or any

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.059
other software from suspicious sites.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.030
Also clicking on a link from a
suspicious email sent from an unknown

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:22.890
email address or even one pretending
to be from a trusted contact.

00:00:23.509 --> 00:00:26.460
The most common signs that a system
has been compromised are when a

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.369
computer slows down, browsers redirect
to other sites, infection warnings

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:36.830
and offers of software to buy to fix
it and pop-up ads, also, problems

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:38.770
shutting down and starting up a system.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.180
Any of these may suggest
that a system is infected.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.719
So how can you stop this happening?

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:51.280
Make sure that your system is protected by
legitimate 'anti-malware' purchased from

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:56.460
a reputable company even if it is a mobile
system and that it is kept up to date,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.019
both the operating system and any software
installed on it such as your web browser.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:06.929
Keep all devices secure and don't download
anything from any dodgy sites or click on

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.379
any unknown links on unreliable emails.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.770
Only purchase from official suppliers.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.230
But if you do find that you have
Malicious software infecting

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:17.289
your system, can it be removed?

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:22.430
It is possible to remove malware, by
running a scan using the security software

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:26.360
installed on the device or system and
taking steps to fix the web browser.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.509
Anti-malware works in two different ways.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.030
The first is a more outdated
approach which works on creating

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.970
a hash of all files on the system.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:39.750
This hash is then checked against a list
of known malicious hashed of malware.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.750
This is referred to as
signature-based detection.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.460
The problem with this method is that
it relies on the fact that the malware

00:01:46.469 --> 00:01:49.940
has been previously identified and
at the pace at which malware is being

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:52.010
developed this is becoming harder to do.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.899
In response to this a lot of antimalware
solutions now work on a heuristic

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:00.940
detection method, which looks more at
the behaviours of files or processes

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:04.960
in a system to identify what could
be potentially malicious behaviour.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.960
--
Nicole: So, what do you do
if your system gets infected?

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.330
The first step in incident response
if you are concerned that a device or

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:16.390
system may be infected is containment.

00:02:16.849 --> 00:02:20.750
It’s important to disconnect from the
internet and the network you’re on as this

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:25.259
will prevent any more data being sent to
a malware server or will stop it spreading

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.050
to other computers on your network.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:32.030
Stay offline as much as possible unless
needing to download any legitimate

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.010
tools to help get rid of the malware.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.209
Disconnect after the download
is complete and stay offline

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.109
until the malware is removed.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:45.170
Opening a system in safe mode or
safe boot allows only the minimum

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:47.109
software and programs to load.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:51.770
Logging in to accounts should be
avoided whilst removing malware so

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:56.330
as not to expose passwords through
copy and paste function or by 'show

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.919
password' because 'key logger' malware
is a common component of malware.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:07.030
Also avoid sharing any personal details or
information whilst a device is infected.

00:03:08.059 --> 00:03:12.850
Check activity monitors for malicious
applications especially if a suspicious

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:15.260
update or application has been installed.

00:03:16.119 --> 00:03:17.550
Run a malware scanner.

00:03:18.049 --> 00:03:22.990
These can remove most standard infections
however if your antivirus software hasn't

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:27.010
already picked this up you should try
another scanner which may be able to

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:32.750
detect more existing and emerging malware
such as a heuristic antimalware solution.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:38.180
Verify the browser homepage this will
involve connecting to the internet and

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:43.049
clear the cache, this is the temporary
storage location where data is saved.

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:48.070
If malware removal is unsuccessful,
it may be that the operating system

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:52.709
may need to be reinstalled along with
applications and programs from scratch.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:57.279
If everything is backed up it shouldn't
be a problem but contacting the system

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.620
suppliers help desk may be necessary.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:05.670
This process is exactly the same for large
companies and organisations but is usually

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:10.330
handled by tools that do these steps
or a dedicated incident response team.

00:04:11.199 --> 00:04:15.579
In this video we have tended to focus
mainly on the single user, how their

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:19.930
system can become infected or suffer
an attack and what to do if it happens.

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:25.179
But often single users link to others
and the attack can gather pace amongst

00:04:25.179 --> 00:04:29.089
their contacts, fellow workmates,
and businesses and organisations.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:32.680
Abraham: Every individual is a
potential target of malicious software

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:36.780
attacks as well as every business or
organisation, no matter what the size.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:42.060
By attacking one individual a threat actor
can have access to so many others and

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.969
the potential to access whole systems.

